        <span style="font-size:11px; font-weight:800; color:var(--accent-teal); text-transform:uppercase;">Why AccessibilityService is Used</span>
        <p style="font-size:13px; line-height:1.5; color:var(--text-secondary);">
          Outloop uses Android’s <strong>AccessibilityService API</strong> strictly to inspect structural view IDs (such as <code>reel_viewer_root</code>) inside apps you explicitly choose, allowing it to pause short-form video feeds while keeping search and messaging usable.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="surface-card" style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px;">
        <span style="font-size:11px; font-weight:800; color:var(--text-primary); text-transform:uppercase;">Zero Data Collection Guarantee</span>
        <p style="font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.5; color:var(--text-secondary);">
          • No keystrokes, passwords, or DM text are ever read.<br/>
          • All intervention counts stay in local Room SQLite.<br/>
          • Network access is restricted to read-only ETag checks for <code>ruleset.json</code>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <a href="settings.html" class="btn-mint" style="display:grid; place-items:center; text-decoration:none;">
      Done
    </a>
  </div>
</body>
</html>

